    "about": {
      "title": "About Mercedes-Benz Engines",
      "logo": "/images/brands/Brand_logo.png",
      "carImage": "/images/brands/Brandpage_about.png",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Mercedes-Benz organises its engines into two code families: OM for diesels and M for petrols. Since 2000, the range has included the OM646 and OM651 four-cylinder diesels fitted across C-Class, E-Class and van models, the OM642 V6 diesel used from the E-Class through to the Sprinter, and petrol families including the M271 four-cylinder and M272 V6. From 2016 the OM654 and OM656 introduced the current diesel generation, while AMG models run their own line from the M156 6.2 V8 to today's M177 4.0 biturbo.",
        "Two things matter when buying a replacement. First, Mercedes engines are application-specific: the same family can differ in sump, turbo arrangement and ancillaries between a saloon, an SUV and a van, so we sell configured units, not generic engines. Second, several modern Mercedes engines are Renault-Nissan sourced — the 1.5 diesel in the A-Class is the Renault K9K and the 1.6 diesel in the C-Class and Vito is the Renault R9M — which we list under their most widely traded names with every Mercedes code cross-referenced, so the engine you find is always the engine that fits."
      ]
    },
    "warrantyDelivery": {
      "title": "Warranty & Delivery on Mercedes Engines",
      "items": [
        {
          "icon": "shield-check",
          "title": "Warranty & returns",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Reconditioned engines carry a 12-month, unlimited-mileage warranty on internal mechanical components; used engines state their warranty term on each listing.",
            "If an engine turns out not to be compatible, return it uninstalled within 14 days for a full refund including original delivery."
          ]
        },
        {
          "icon": "truck",
          "title": "Delivery",
          "paragraphs": [
            "UK mainland delivery by kerbside pallet, typically 2–4 working days for in-stock units, with tracking emailed on dispatch.",
            "Van and V6 units ship on heavy-duty pallets at no extra cost — the delivery price shown at checkout is the price you pay."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "faqs": {
      "title": "Mercedes Engine Buying FAQs",
      "subtitle": "Answers to the most common questions about buying a Mercedes engine from GMC.",
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "Which Mercedes-Benz engines do you sell?",
          "a": "We cover 27 Mercedes engine families spanning every UK model from 2000 to the present — diesel families like the OM651, OM642 and OM646, petrol families like the M271, M272 and M276, the AMG range from the M156 to the M177, and the Renault-shared units fitted to compact models and vans. Each engine is sold as an application-specific unit verified for your exact vehicle."
        },
        {
          "q": "Are your Mercedes engines used or reconditioned?",
